---
// /blueprint — the blueprint sheets. One idea, one sheet, plain words on the drawing: things a
// person could redraw to explain the idea to someone else. Drawn by tools/sheets.mjs (one file
// per sheet in tools/sheets/); add a row here when a sheet is added.
import { VERSION, BUILD } from '../lib/version';
import PhoneNav from '../components/PhoneNav.astro';

const SHEETS: { n: number; file: string; title: string; sub: string; href?: string; label?: string; where: string; misleads: string }[] = [
  { n: 1, file: "sheet-1-the-coil", title: "How things get better", sub: "without using more stuff", href: "/open/NOTES-circular-to-helical", where: "From circular to helical", misleads: "The coil has no scale on its upward axis: nobody can yet measure “more you can do next”." },
  { n: 2, file: "sheet-2-the-bus", title: "A better seat on the bus", sub: "is not the same as a longer trip", href: "/open/NOTES-worse-for-none", where: "“Worse for none”, §4", misleads: "A passenger can say the edge is after their stop. And “more road” is one phrase for several different things." },
  { n: 3, file: "sheet-3-the-jar", title: "The sun is pay", sub: "coal, oil and gas are savings: they spend once", href: "/explore#energy-income-inheritance", where: "energy-income-inheritance", misleads: "The jar suggests we can see how much is left. Nobody knows the level exactly; running out is more like the bottom getting harder to reach." },
  { n: 4, file: "sheet-4-the-well", title: "A full well with the lid on", sub: "is not the same as water to drink", href: "/explore#held-value-not-reachable", where: "held-value-not-reachable", misleads: "Lifting the lid looks as if it makes more water. It may only move the same water around. And water is used up when drunk, where knowledge is not." },
  { n: 5, file: "sheet-5-the-stepping-stones", title: "What a stone is worth", sub: "the ways on it leaves you, one step at a time", href: "/explore#value-option-space", where: "value-option-space, option-space-as-chess-moves", misleads: "The stones are fixed and easy to count. Real options cannot be counted, and one person’s step can sink stones for someone else." },
  { n: 6, file: "sheet-6-the-stump", title: "Broken fast, built slow", sub: "so a seedling does not pay for the tree", href: "/explore#asymmetry-of-option-space-change", where: "asymmetry-of-option-space-change", misleads: "A tree suggests every loss is someone choosing to cut and every rebuild is slow. Some builds are fast and some losses are slow." },
  { n: 7, file: "sheet-7-the-hen", title: "A full basket of eggs", sub: "is not the same as the hen that lays them", href: "/open/NOTES-worse-for-none", where: "“Worse for none”, §5", misleads: "The hen is easy to see in the drawing. In life the thing that makes more is the hard part to see, and it drains bit by bit, not all at once. The ranking on the sheet is a proposal, still argued." },
  { n: 8, file: "sheet-8-the-bridge", title: "People just use a bridge", sub: "so ask who it reaches, and what carries the rest", href: "/open/NOTES-recursive-fitness-and-bridge-test", where: "The bridge test", misleads: "A bridge is built once by someone with the money to build it. The picture is quiet about who that is." },
  { n: 9, file: "sheet-9-the-plank", title: "A try is not a change", sub: "draw lots of lines. the rule is for the cut.", href: "/open/NOTES-worse-for-none", where: "“Worse for none”, §2", misleads: "A saw cut is one person, one cut, for ever. Real changes reach other people and are not always permanent, and a small trial in the world is itself a small change." },
  { n: 10, file: "sheet-10-the-steps", title: "Your reach, not your lead", sub: "what this keeps safe, and what it doesn’t", href: "/open/NOTES-worse-for-none", where: "“Worse for none”, §4 and objection 5", misleads: "The steps look free; someone made and paid for them. And where the good things are scarce, being ahead is part of your reach." },
  { n: 11, file: "sheet-11-the-receipt", title: "The cost that lands", sub: "somewhere else, or later", href: "/open/NOTES-razor-blade-case", where: "displaced-costs and the razor-blade case", misleads: "A receipt makes the rest of the bill look like one line that could simply be added. Often nobody knows its size, or who will be handed it." },
  { n: 12, file: "sheet-12-the-lantern", title: "Choose from where you stand", sub: "take the best step from here, then look again", href: "/explore#option-space-as-chess-moves", where: "option-space-as-chess-moves (after Dave Snowden)", misleads: "The ground stands still and the lantern lights the same distance every way. Real ground shifts with time, and there is more than one walker." },
  { n: 13, file: "sheet-13-the-bath", title: "GDP watches the tap", sub: "not how full the bath is", href: "/explore#throughput-cost", where: "throughput-cost, money-as-signal", misleads: "A bath has one water level you could simply read off. What is left to live on is many different things, and nobody agrees how to add them into one number." },
  { n: 14, file: "sheet-14-the-fence", title: "A fence at the top", sub: "costs less than the ambulance, and is harder to see", href: "/explore#prevention-over-repair", where: "prevention-over-repair", misleads: "Here everyone can see where the cliff is and that a fence would work. Often nobody knows where the edge is, or which fence stops which fall, and some fences cost more than the falls they stop." },
  { n: 15, file: "sheet-15-the-tide", title: "A rising tide", sub: "lifts the boats, and hides the rocks", href: "/explore#growth-masks-strain", where: "growth-masks-strain", misleads: "A tide lifts every boat by the same amount and goes out on its own. Growth lifts some far more than others, and whether it slows is partly chosen." },
  { n: 16, file: "sheet-16-the-room", title: "A floor and a roof", sub: "nobody falls through one, nothing breaks through the other", href: "/lineage", label: "Whose idea it is", where: "Kate Raworth, Doughnut Economics; a neighbour’s idea, drawn as fairly as we can", misleads: "A roof and a floor are single lines you can see. Hers are many separate limits, some known far better than others, and the roof does not give way in one place at one moment." },
  { n: 17, file: "sheet-17-the-chain", title: "The good of all is multiplied", sub: "not added up: leave anyone at nothing, and it comes to nothing", href: "/lineage", label: "Whose idea it is", where: "Stefano Zamagni with Luigino Bruni, the civil economy; a neighbour’s idea, drawn as fairly as we can", misleads: "A chain runs in a line, each link holding only the next. People hold one another in many directions at once, and a real society does not fall the moment one person is failed, which is why it can go on failing them." },
  { n: 18, file: "sheet-18-the-boat", title: "A company that belongs", sub: "to what it is for, not to whoever can buy it", label: "Whose idea it is", where: "Steward-ownership, after the Purpose network. A neighbour’s idea, drawn as fairly as we can; not argued here.", misleads: "A flag says what the boat is for and never changes. The drawing is quiet about who chooses the next steerer, who can remove a bad one, and how a boat nobody can buy raises the money for a bigger one." },
  { n: 19, file: "sheet-19-the-mill-stream", title: "Let the money go round", sub: "turn the town’s own wheels before it leaves", label: "Whose idea it is", where: "Community wealth building, after Neil McInroy, CLES and the Democracy Collaborative. A neighbour’s idea, drawn as fairly as we can; not argued here.", misleads: "Water turns every wheel it passes for free. A local firm may cost more or do the job worse, and money kept in one town is money that does not reach the next." },
  { n: 20, file: "sheet-20-the-one-roof", title: "Too small alone", sub: "so the village owns one co-op that runs them all", label: "Whose idea it is", where: "The community co-operative, after Giovanni Teneggi and the co-ops of the Apennines. A neighbour’s idea, drawn as fairly as we can; not argued here.", misleads: "One roof looks tidy and settled. If the busy part fails, everything under the roof goes with it, and the drawing is quiet about the years of unpaid work it takes to get there." },
  { n: 21, file: "sheet-21-the-watering-can", title: "Most need, least care", sub: "good care tends to go where it’s least needed", label: "Whose idea it is", where: "The inverse care law, after Julian Tudor Hart (The Lancet, 1971). A neighbour’s idea, drawn as fairly as we can; not argued here.", misleads: "One gardener looks like one person choosing badly. The law is about thousands of small choices, none of them meant, and care is not one thing poured from one can." },
  { n: 22, file: "sheet-22-the-tent", title: "Room for everybody", sub: "made by doing more with less", href: "/lineage", label: "Whose idea it is", where: "Buckminster Fuller; one of this work’s two direct debts", misleads: "Five people fit in a tent easily. The picture does not show eight billion, and doing a job with less stuff has often meant the job simply gets done more, using more in total." },
  { n: 23, file: "sheet-23-the-rope", title: "A game to keep going", sub: "not every game is played to be won", href: "/explore#infinite-game", label: "Whose idea it is", where: "James Carse; the other direct debt, argued here as infinite-game", misleads: "A skipping game is friendly and anyone can walk away. Real games to keep going have people in them playing to win, and many cannot leave." },
  { n: 24, file: "sheet-24-the-bicycle", title: "What a bike is worth", sub: "is what it lets this person do and be", href: "/lineage", label: "Whose idea it is", where: "Amartya Sen, the capability approach; a near neighbour of value-option-space", misleads: "Three roads are easy to count. Sen never gave a list of what counts or a way to add it up, and the drawing makes it look as if he did." }
];
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>The blueprint — Configuration Economics</title>
    <meta name="description" content="A living blueprint for a world that works for everybody, one hand-drawn sheet per idea." />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Cormorant+Garamond:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;1,400&family=Sora:wght@300;400;500&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style is:global>
      :root { --void:#0a0a0c; --text-primary:#e8e8f0; --text-secondary:#a0a0b8; --text-muted:#606080; --accent:#4a9eff; --font-display:'Cormorant Garamond',serif; --font-body:'Sora',sans-serif; --font-mono:'JetBrains Mono',monospace; }
      * { margin:0; padding:0; box-sizing:border-box; }
      body { font-family:var(--font-body); background:var(--void); color:var(--text-primary); min-height:100vh; line-height:1.7; }
      .top-nav { position:fixed; top:0; left:0; right:0; height:56px; background:rgba(10,10,12,0.95); backdrop-filter:blur(12px); border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.06); display:flex; align-items:center; gap:2rem; padding:0 2rem; z-index:100; }
      .nav-home { font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:1.125rem; color:var(--text-primary); text-decoration:none; }
      .nav-link { font-size:0.875rem; color:var(--text-secondary); text-decoration:none; }
      .nav-link:hover { color:var(--accent); }
      .nav-right { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:1rem; margin-left:auto; flex-wrap:wrap; }
      .nav-version { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.75rem; color:var(--accent); }
      .nav-build { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.75rem; color:var(--text-muted); opacity:0.7; }
      main { max-width:1080px; margin:0 auto; padding:100px 2rem 6rem; }
      h1 { font-family:var(--font-display); font-weight:400; font-size:2.6rem; line-height:1.15; margin:0 0 0.6rem; }
      .lede { color:var(--text-secondary); max-width:640px; margin:0 0 2.5rem; }
      .grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr); gap:2.5rem 2rem; }
      @media (min-width:700px) { .grid { grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); } }
      .sheet a.pic { display:block; border-radius:6px; overflow:hidden; box-shadow:0 10px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.45); }
      .sheet img { display:block; width:100%; height:auto; }
      .sheet-n { font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.62rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; color:var(--accent); margin-top:0.9rem; }
      .sheet-title { font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:1.35rem; line-height:1.25; color:var(--text-primary); margin:0.1rem 0 0.35rem; }
      .sheet-title span { color:var(--text-secondary); font-style:italic; }
      .sheet p { color:var(--text-secondary); font-size:0.85rem; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 0.35rem; }
      .sheet p strong { color:var(--text-primary); font-weight:400; }
      .sheet p a { color:var(--accent); text-decoration:none; }
      @media (max-width:640px) { main { padding-left:1.25rem; padding-right:1.25rem; } h1 { font-size:2.1rem; } }
    </style>
      <PhoneNav />
  </head>
  <body>
    <nav class="top-nav">
      <a href="/" class="nav-home">Configuration Economics</a>
      <div class="nav-right">
        <a href="/open" class="nav-link">Open</a>
        <a href="/explore" class="nav-link">Propositions</a>
        <span class="nav-version">{VERSION}</span>
        <span class="nav-build">build {BUILD}</span>
      </div>
    </nav>
    <main>
      <h1>A living blueprint for a world that works for everybody</h1>
      <p class="lede">One idea, one sheet, in plain words: drawings a person could redraw to explain the idea to someone else. Like everything else here they are works in progress, added to and improved as we go. Every picture misleads somewhere, so each sheet says where. Tap a sheet to see it full size.</p>
      <div class="grid">
        {SHEETS.map(s => (
          <div class="sheet" id={s.file}>
            <a class="pic" href={`/sheets/${s.file}.svg`}><img src={`/sheets/${s.file}.svg`} width="780" height="1240" loading="lazy" alt={`Hand-drawn blueprint sheet ${s.n}: ${s.title}, ${s.sub}`} /></a>
            <div class="sheet-n">Sheet {s.n}</div>
            <div class="sheet-title">{s.title} <span>{s.sub}</span></div>
            <p><strong>{s.label ?? "Where it is argued"}:</strong> {s.href ? <a href={s.href}>{s.where} &rarr;</a> : s.where}</p>
            <p><strong>Where the picture misleads:</strong> {s.misleads}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
